    <section class="content-container" id="about-main-content">
      <h1>OUR MISSION</h1>

      <div>
        <p>
          Sidus Robotics is committed to advancing robotics in space while
          providing students at Memorial University with valuable hands-on
          experience. Beyond skill development, our mission is to position
          Memorial University as a hub for innovation in robotics and space
          exploration. By competing in the Canadian International Rover
          Challenge (CIRC) we push the boundaries of research and technology.
          Teams participating in CIRC tackle real-world challenges by simulating
          early space settlement scenarios on extraterrestrial terrain, testing
          their rovers in dynamic and demanding environments. Depending on their
          chosen division, teams compete in either winter or summer events,
          proving their rover's capabilities in different conditions. Through
          this project, Sidus Robotics is not only preparing the next generation
          of engineers and innovators but also showcasing Newfoundland and
          Memorial University on the national stage.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="content-container" id="about-secondary-content">
      <h1>UP AND COMING</h1>

      <div class="container">
        <p>
          The Canadian International Rover Challenge (CIRC) is a
          university-level competition that challenges students to design,
          build, and test a rover capable of operating in Mars-like conditions.
          Hosted by the Canadian Space Technology Advancement Group (CSTAG), the
          competition fosters innovation in space robotics while providing
          students with hands-on experience in mechanical design, electronics,
          and software development. Throughout the challenge, teams must
          simulate real-world space exploration scenarios, tackling complex
          tasks such as autonomous navigation, object manipulation, and terrain
          traversal. Sidus Robotics is excited to take on this challenge,
          representing Memorial University and contributing to the future of
          space technology.
        </p>

        <div class="container">
          <a href="https://circ.cstag.ca/"
            ><img loading="lazy" src={CIRC.src} alt="" /></a
          >
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

